# Security

## Secrets

Never commit:

- API keys
- OpenAI keys
- Tokens
- Passwords
- Credentials
- Private keys

Use environment variables.

## Frontend Environment

Never expose server-side secrets through frontend environment variables.

Only variables explicitly intended for the browser may be exposed.

## OpenAI

The OpenAI API key must remain on the backend.

The frontend must never call OpenAI directly.

## RAG

The frontend must never directly access:

- ChromaDB
- Vector store credentials
- LlamaIndex configuration
- Embedding providers
- LLM provider credentials

## User Input

Treat user input as untrusted.

Do not render user-generated content as raw HTML unless there is an explicit sanitization strategy.

## API Errors

Do not expose internal backend details.

Do not display:

- Stack traces
- SQL errors
- Provider errors
- Internal exception messages

## Logging

Do not log:

- API keys
- Authentication tokens
- Sensitive user data

## Dependencies

Do not add packages with unclear provenance.

Keep dependencies minimal.

## Environment Files

`.env` files containing secrets must not be committed.

`.env.example` may contain variable names and safe example values.

Never put real credentials in `.env.example`.